  "articleBody": "Installing soft-close drawers can really elevate your home, but there are a few common pitfalls that can turn a smooth project into a headache. Here are some mistakes to steer clear of: \n1. **Installing slides too tightly:** This is a big one! If the slides are jammed in, your drawer won't glide properly, or the soft-close mechanism might not engage. Always ensure a little wiggle room. \n2. **Skipping pre-drilling:** Don't just screw directly into your cabinet or drawer. Pre-drilling prevents wood splitting and helps ensure your screws go in straight and flush. \n3. **Failing to check for obstructions:** Before you finalize everything, open and close the drawer a few times. Make sure nothing inside the cabinet or on the drawer itself is getting in the way. \n4. **Not ensuring flush screw heads:** Any screw head that isn't completely flush can catch on the drawer or cabinet, causing binding and preventing smooth operation. \n5. **Not fully seating or adjusting the soft-close mechanism:** Sometimes the soft-close part needs a little nudge or adjustment to work perfectly. Don't assume it's good to go until you've tested it repeatedly. \n6. **Ignoring out-of-square cabinets:** If your cabinets aren't perfectly square, it makes getting the slides level incredibly difficult. This is where professional help, like HH Remodeling LLC, can really save you a lot of grief.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
